            <ArticleTitle>[Rectus sheath hematoma--detection of hemorrhage of ruptured aneurysm of the epigastric artery in CT].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of rectus sheath hematoma is described. Computed tomography demonstrated a still active bleeding from an aneurysm which was situated at the junction of the inferior and superior epigastric artery. The recognition of a continuous hemorrhage contributed to the decision of an immediate surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
